  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, PCA-2000 + ResNet50, concat) is the best result so far (Acc 0.527, F1 0.510), showing a ~4.2 pp gain over RNA-only (config_001, Acc 0.485) and confirming that fusion adds value despite the weak image-only baseline (config_010, Acc 0.208). Uncertainty: we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat); it is unclear whether weighted fusion would improve or degrade performance, and whether the fusion mechanism is a meaningful design axis worth further exploration. This experiment (config_017) is a clean single-variable ablation from config_016—changing only fusion from concat to weighted—so any performance difference can be attributed to the fusion strategy. Under a limited budget, this is the most informative next step: if weighted fusion helps, it validates a family of weighted configs (019, 021, etc.); if it does not, we can rule out fusion strategy as a key lever and redirect budget toward higher-impact dimensions (multiprofile, stronger encoders)."
}

